        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "In the radiological examination, the victim's age has been opined to be 18 years and no injury or mark of use of force has been found on her body.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1770,
      "end": 1916,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "In her statement recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C., the victim stated that on 03.09.2022 her mother had beaten her for this reason she left her and went to the applicant at Ahmadabad.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1917,
      "end": 2102,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 164",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1950,
          "end": 1961
        },
        {
          "text": "Cr.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1962,
          "end": 1969
        },
        {
          "text": "03.09.2022",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1997,
          "end": 2007
        },
        {
          "text": "Ahmadabad",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 2092,
          "end": 2101
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "A copy of the relevant extract of Parivar Register annexed with a supplementary affidavit filed on behalf of the applicant indicates that victim's year of birth is 2002 Having considered the aforesaid facts and circumstances of the case and keeping in view the facts that from the Parivar register, as also from the radio logical examination report, victim appears to be major and she has consistently stated that she had gone to Ahmadabad alone and at Ahmadabad she stayed with the applicant out of her own free will, I am of the view that the applicant is entitled to be enlarged on bail in the aforesaid case.\nAccordingly, this bail application stands allowed.\nLet the applicant Ram Vishal Verma be released on bail in Case Crime no. 308 of 2022, under Section 363, 366, 376 I.P.C. and Section 3/4 of the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act,\nregistered at Police Station Gauriganj, District Amethi on furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of magistrate/court concerned, subject to following conditions: -\n(i) the applicant shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence;\n(ii) the applicant shall not pressurize the prosecution witnesses;\n(iii) the applicant shall appear on each and every date fixed by the trial court.\nIn case of breach of any of the above conditions, the prosecution shall be at liberty to move bail cancellation application before this Court.\n.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2103,
      "end": 3533,
